Overlay patch 0032: visionOS is Metal-only — no ENABLE_OPENGL
(VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK Phase 01; = sibling ports' visionos-no-opengl).
visionOS has neither desktop GL (glew) nor GLES frameworks, so LUS's OpenGL
comparator backend cannot compile there. Upstream already guards the whole
backend behind ENABLE_OPENGL; this stops defining it when SOH_VISIONOS is set.
iOS unchanged (that branch never defines ENABLE_OPENGL anyway; defensive).

--- a/libultraship/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libultraship/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -280,7 +280,8 @@
     endif()
 else()
     target_compile_definitions(libultraship PRIVATE
-        ENABLE_OPENGL
+        # SOH_IOS (overlay 0032): no GL of any kind on visionOS — Metal only.
+        $<$<NOT:$<BOOL:${SOH_VISIONOS}>>:ENABLE_OPENGL>
         $<$<CONFIG:Debug>:_DEBUG>
         $<$<NOT:$<CONFIG:Debug>>:NDEBUG>
         $<$<CONFIG:Debug>:SPDLOG_ACTIVE_LEVEL=0>
